<version>1.0.0</version>
<language>Rust</language>
Output src/conventions.rs. Manual implementation; provider regeneration unverified.
Use existing Coefficient, Polynomial, Budget, computation::Result only.
Expose EpsilonConvention::{Library,MonoNotes}; Copy,Clone,Debug,Eq,PartialEq.
R1 MUST: upper12/lower12 return (+1,-1) for Library and (-1,+1) for MonoNotes.
R2 MUST: raise and lower apply epsilon matrices to ordered (1,2) components;
raise(v)=upper12*(v[1],-v[0]), lower(v)=lower12*(v[1],-v[0]).
R3 MUST: bracket(a,c)=upper12*(a[0]*c[1]-a[1]*c[0]) for commuting components.
R4 MUST: convert_lower(self,target,v,b) keeps lower components fixed;
convert_upper multiplies upper components by self.upper12()*target.upper12().
Lowering converted upper components with target recovers original lower components.
R5 MUST: all polynomial APIs are generic over Coefficient and accept a mutable
shared Budget, returning computation::Result. Even identity conversions validate
resource limits. No panic arithmetic or backend narrowing.
R6 MUST NOT: choose a default profile, migrate existing callers, edit notes, or
interpret commuting determinants as Grassmann field bilinears.
Signatures: upper12/lower12(self)->i64 (const); raise/lower/convert_lower/
convert_upper -> Result<[Polynomial<A>;2]>; bracket -> Result<Polynomial<A>>.
Vector parameters are borrowed arrays; conversion target follows self.
